Modifications made by SOCIS
---------------------------
Required by Apache-2.0 section 4(b):

  1. Frontmatter rewritten to the SOCIS skill schema (`metadata.socis`),
     preserving upstream `author` and `license` fields.
  2. Descriptions shortened to <=60 characters for the SOCIS prompt index.
     Full upstream descriptions remain in each skill's body and references/.
  3. Subdomain filtering — only the subdomains listed in
     scripts/vendor_security_skills.py were vendored.
  4. Unreferenced `scripts/` directories removed. Upstream ships a scripts/
     folder with every skill, but 714 of 765 skill procedures never invoke
     theirs. Those were deleted; the 49 whose SKILL.md actually calls a script
     retain it. No skill procedure, reference file, or asset was altered.

Review status
-------------
Skill procedures and reference material are vendored as-is and have NOT been
individually reviewed by SOCIS. Review any skill before relying on it in a
customer engagement.

Executable content was reduced from 1,033 third-party Python files to 80,
retained only where a skill's documented workflow invokes them. Those 49
scripts are third-party code and should be reviewed before use in a customer
environment.

Six skills reference scripts that upstream never shipped
(detecting-aws-credential-exposure-with-trufflehog, implementing-api-schema-
validation-security, implementing-secret-scanning-with-gitleaks,
performing-web-application-vulnerability-triage, unbroker). Those references
were already broken upstream and are unaffected by the changes above.
